ROAST.PET PERSONALISATION GOLD =E2=80=94 CUSTOMER-SIGNAL DELTA

Prior Sent state recovered through the 19:47 report. I rejected semantic
duplicates unless new independent evidence materially strengthened a
cluster.

1 MATERIAL SIGNAL

CLUSTER: animation controllability / mouth geometry preservation
Platform: Talking Pet AI customer reviews (App Store-derived review corpus)
Source: https://mwm.ai/apps/talking-pet-ai-cat-dog-talk/6479892860
Date: 2026-02-18
Customer language: The reviewer says the app does not preserve the
character of their animals, that =E2=80=9CThe mouth does not move properly,=
=E2=80=9D and
specifically complains that =E2=80=9CYou can=E2=80=99t make [the] mouth sma=
ller or larger.=E2=80=9D
They also report a horse being transformed into a dog and generated
backgrounds differing from the preview.
Wanted/problem: The buyer wants animation to preserve the individual animal
and wants control over a conspicuously wrong talking-mouth effect rather
than accepting a one-shot render.
Current workaround/product: Talking Pet AI automatic facial animation.
Roast.pet implication: Add a post-motion-preview correction primitive
specifically for MOUTH: smaller / normal / larger, plus =E2=80=9Cmouth look=
s wrong=E2=80=9D
regenerate. Treat mouth geometry as an identity landmark rather than
generic lip-sync. Preserve the approved background/scene as a locked
constraint as well.
Occasion/audience: Talking-pet videos; broad pet-owner gift/entertainment
audience.
Independent elsewhere: YES. Prior state already contains independent
complaints about poor talking-mouth quality and the need to preview motion
before payment. This evidence materially strengthens that cluster because
it identifies a concrete customer-requested control: mouth size.
Confidence: HIGH
Prototype/test: After the 2=E2=80=933 second motion proof, show three one-t=
ap
corrections only if rejected: MOUTH TOO BIG / MOUTH TOO SMALL / DOESN=E2=80=
=99T
LOOK LIKE MY PET. Measure rescue rate versus generic regenerate.
Decision: BUILD/TEST

WHY THIS IS NEW
The prior evidence established that a still likeness can fail once animated
and that customers want to see motion before commitment. This review goes
one step further: it names an adjustment the customer wishes existed. That
converts =E2=80=9Cpreview the animation=E2=80=9D into =E2=80=9Cpreview + co=
nstrained correction,=E2=80=9D
which is much more actionable.

RECURRING-CLUSTER STATE =E2=80=94 directional counts from accepted independ=
ent
evidence

   - Exact likeness / identity preservation: very strong, repeatedly
   independently supported
   - Motion/talking fidelity: strong and strengthening; now includes
   explicit mouth-size control demand
   - Preview/approval before final: strong
   - Better source-photo guidance: strong
   - Fast/digital/last-minute delivery: strong
   - Multi-pet: strong
   - Personality/essence capture: strong
   - Revision/control without friction: strong and strengthening
   - Authentic pet audio: moderate
   - QR/physical+digital reveal: moderate
   - Memorial: moderate, but memorial-with-humor remains UNKNOWN
   - Editable jokes / recipient-specific roast: plausible product fit but
   direct demand evidence remains weaker than likeness evidence
   - Kid/adult roast modes: UNKNOWN
   - Sports/work-colleague roast: UNKNOWN

TOP 5 CUSTOMER REQUESTS TO PRODUCTIZE

   1. Exact individual-pet likeness that survives animation.
   2. Preview/approve before final commitment, including a motion proof.
   3. Simple correction controls when the talking mouth or identity looks
   wrong.
   4. Clear source-photo guidance with buyer control over the primary
   reference.
   5. Fast digital delivery / last-minute path, with physical fulfillment
   optional.

STRONGEST UNMET NEED
A talking-pet gift that remains recognizably the exact animal during
speech=E2=80=94not merely a convincing dog/cat animation.

EASIEST CONVERSION-LIFT CHANGE
On motion-preview rejection, replace a blank revision box with MOUTH TOO
BIG / MOUTH TOO SMALL / DOESN=E2=80=99T LOOK LIKE MY PET. This converts a k=
nown
complaint into a low-friction recovery path.

BEST NEW ETSY LISTING/PRODUCT IDEA FROM CUSTOMER LANGUAGE
=E2=80=9CYour Dog Roasts Them =E2=80=94 Preview Your Pet Talking + Fix the =
Mouth Before
Final Video =E2=80=94 Personalized Birthday Video + QR Card.=E2=80=9D The l=
isting promise
should emphasize identity preservation rather than generic AI animation.

IMPORTANT NEGATIVE SIGNAL
Do not assume a state-of-the-art talking model eliminates the need for
correction UX. Customers notice small mouth-geometry errors intensely, and
automatic animation can make an otherwise recognizable pet feel wrong. A
one-shot =E2=80=98regenerate=E2=80=99 button is weaker than targeted correc=
tions.

SEARCH NOTE
This run reviewed current talking-pet customer reviews plus
personalized-pet, multi-pet, last-minute, QR/video and likeness evidence.
Most findings were semantic repeats of already accepted clusters and were
rejected from the delta.

